# The constraint surface: the files that decide what CI accepts.
#
# Agents write to the same tree these live in, so a change blocked by a gate
# could loosen the gate in the same PR. Two defences, one mechanical and one
# human: `Ratchet / Constraints` (scripts/check-constraint-growth.py) rejects any
# loosening of the declarations against the base branch, and this file requires
# a human owner's review on every change to a gate, a baseline, a declaration,
# or a workflow. Enable "Require review from Code Owners" on main for the second
# half to bind.

# The gates themselves and the workflows that run them
/.github/                                    @ethenotethan
/scripts/check-*.py                          @ethenotethan
/scripts/collect-*.py                        @ethenotethan
/scripts/build_architecture.py               @ethenotethan
/scripts/test_architecture.py                @ethenotethan
/scripts/test_constraint_growth.py           @ethenotethan
/Makefile                                    @ethenotethan

# Frozen baselines (already compared against main by the ratchets)
/metrics-baseline.json                       @ethenotethan
/perf-baseline.json                          @ethenotethan
/.swiftlint-baseline                         @ethenotethan
/.gitleaksignore                             @ethenotethan

# Rule definitions
/.swiftlint.yml                              @ethenotethan
/.gitleaks.toml                              @ethenotethan
/Tests/PortalTests/ArchitectureTests.swift   @ethenotethan

# Declared architecture: invariants, fail-closed declarations, specifications
/architecture/config.json                    @ethenotethan
/architecture/interplay/invariants.json      @ethenotethan
/architecture/interplay/overlay.json         @ethenotethan
/architecture/specifications/                @ethenotethan
/docs/architecture-rules.md                  @ethenotethan
